## 10. PRIVACY AND SECURITY

All tools should process user data locally in the browser whenever possible.

Do not transmit user files or text to an external service.

Do not add:
- Analytics that send data externally.
- Advertising scripts.
- Tracking pixels.
- Hidden network requests.
- External file uploads.
- User accounts.
- Unnecessary cookies.
- Unnecessary local storage.
- Secret collection forms.

Do not save sensitive input in browser storage.

Use local storage only for harmless preferences if genuinely necessary.

For any feature that loads a third-party library, explain the relevant dependency and avoid sending user content to that library's external services.

For HTML previews, use sandboxed iframes and appropriate security restrictions.

For password generation, use crypto.getRandomValues().

For hashing, use Web Crypto API where supported.

For file processing, validate input and manage memory responsibly.

